    website: "https://researchmap.jp/kidoishi/"
abstract: >-
  This dataset presents a small TEI P5 and IIIF implementation for the opening
  of Farīd al-Dīn ʿAṭṭār's Manṭiq al-ṭayr, based on two manuscript witnesses.
  It contains a diplomatic transcription of 30 couplets in BnF Persan 348
  (dated 1492), a separate transcription of the corresponding nine opening
  couplets in Smithsonian FSC-MS-28 (sixteenth century), and links from 78
  hemistichs to regions in three IIIF Canvases. Automated collation of the 18
  overlapping hemistichs records 16 exact matches, one textual variant, and one
  passage partly covered by physical repair. The package includes a
  project-specific TEI customization, generated IIIF AnnotationPages,
  validation scripts and reports, and a browser-based comparison viewer. This
  is a technical and methodological prototype, not a critical edition. The
  author checked the transcriptions and image regions against the manuscript
  images; the work has not undergone independent scholarly review. Manuscript
  images are referenced through IIIF and are not included in the package.
keywords:
